--TEST--
Every `Core\Os` fact is stable across two reads in one program — the three identities are equal, `residentBytes` only ever grows, and `loadAverage` answers both times or neither — `rule:core-api/tier-roster`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// The invariance the shape case cannot see: a member that read a fresh figure
// out of the wrong place, or cached one it should not have, still answers
// plausibly the first time. Asked twice in one process, a pid, a hostname and
// a core count are the same answer or the member is wrong.
uint $firstPid = Core\Os::pid();
uint $secondPid = Core\Os::pid();
if ($firstPid == $secondPid) {
    echo "pid: the same process\n";
} else {
    echo "pid: two processes\n";
}

string $firstHost = Core\Os::hostname();
string $secondHost = Core\Os::hostname();
if ($firstHost == $secondHost) {
    echo "hostname: the same host\n";
} else {
    echo "hostname: two hosts\n";
}

uint $firstCores = Core\Os::cpuCount();
uint $secondCores = Core\Os::cpuCount();
if ($firstCores == $secondCores) {
    echo "cpuCount: the same fleet\n";
} else {
    echo "cpuCount: a fleet that changed size\n";
}

// The one fact here that is *not* required to be equal, and the difference is
// the member's whole reading: a resident high-water mark can only grow, so a
// second answer below the first would mean this reports what the process holds
// right now — which is `Core\Budget::memoryHeld`'s question and not this one
// (ADR 0148 § 12).
uint $firstResident = Core\Os::residentBytes();
uint $secondResident = Core\Os::residentBytes();
if ($secondResident >= $firstResident) {
    echo "residentBytes: a high-water mark\n";
} else {
    echo "residentBytes: a figure that fell\n";
}

// A member does not answer sometimes: whether this platform keeps a load
// average is a fact about the platform, so two calls agree even here. Summing
// the figures counted is what makes one answer and one refusal visible — 3 is
// the sum neither branch below accepts.
uint $counted = 0;
try {
    var $first = Core\Os::loadAverage();
    $counted = $counted + Core\Arr::count($first);
} catch (RuntimeError $refused) {
    echo "";
}
try {
    var $second = Core\Os::loadAverage();
    $counted = $counted + Core\Arr::count($second);
} catch (RuntimeError $refused) {
    echo "";
}
if ($counted == 6 || $counted == 0) {
    echo "loadAverage: both times or neither\n";
} else {
    echo "loadAverage: once\n";
}
--EXPECT--
pid: the same process
hostname: the same host
cpuCount: the same fleet
residentBytes: a high-water mark
loadAverage: both times or neither
